    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0339" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9491/25</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-23">March 23, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador<anchor n="85" xml:id="d379-f1"/> called to see me this
                    evening at my request.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador brought up the question of the continued diplomatic representation
                    of Japan in Tehran. He said that his Government had learned that Japan intended
                    materially to increase diplomatic representation in that capital for purposes
                    which, of course, <pb facs="0340" n="328" xml:id="pg328"/> were obvious. He
                    requested that a further message be sent to our Minister in Tehran urging him to
                    request again that the Iranian Government sever diplomatic relations with Japan,
                    and that this Government use as a leverage the economic assistance which the
                    Iranian Government was requesting of us. I said I would be glad to have a
                    further message sent to our Minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d379-f1" n="85" xml:id="d379-f1-content">
                <p>Viscount Halifax.</p>
